---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { GITHUB_URL, HERDR_URL, HERDR_VERSION, INSTALL_COMMAND, LICENSE_URL } from '../lib/site'
---

<Base>
  <main>
    <h1>grasslands</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A native macOS app for <a href={HERDR_URL}>herdr</a>. It gives your agents a real window:
      workspaces, tabs and splits, a Ghostty terminal in every pane, a file tree and editor that
      follow the focused agent's worktree, and live agent status.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      herdr keeps running the agents, terminals and sessions as a headless server. grasslands
      replaces its terminal UI and talks to it over the socket API.
    </p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <div class="install">
      <pre id="install-command">{INSTALL_COMMAND}</pre>
      <button type="button" data-copy="install-command" hidden>Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Needs macOS and herdr {HERDR_VERSION}.</p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Mirrors herdr's workspaces, tabs and split layouts both ways. Splitting, closing, moving
        panes and dragging dividers all go through herdr.
      </li>
      <li>Runs a real Ghostty terminal for each herdr pane.</li>
      <li>
        Follows the focused pane to its git worktree, even after an agent runs <code>cd</code>. The file
        tree re-roots there, respects <code>.gitignore</code> and updates as agents write files.
      </li>
      <li>
        Opens files in a tabbed editor. Files an agent changes on disk reload, and it asks first if
        you have unsaved edits.
      </li>
      <li>
        Lists every workspace in the sidebar with its agents, blocked ones first. Create, rename and
        close workspaces and worktrees from there.
      </li>
      <li>A command palette for app commands and herdr plugin actions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      Alpha. This is v0. It sends real commands to herdr, so closing a pane kills its process. It
      asks first when an agent is working. Expect rough edges. The <a
        href={`${GITHUB_URL}#known-gaps`}>known gaps</a
      > are listed in the README.
    </p>

    <h2>Links</h2>
    <ul class="links">
      <li><a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href={HERDR_URL}>herdr.dev</a></li>
      <li><a href={LICENSE_URL}>MIT license</a></li>
    </ul>
  </main>

  <script>
    for (const button of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]')) {
      const source = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy ?? '')
      if (!source || !navigator.clipboard) continue
      button.hidden = false
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(source.textContent ?? '')
        button.textContent = 'Copied'
        setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy'), 1500)
      })
    }
  </script>
</Base>
